(Postmortem INC-7750: cart-api thread pool starvation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Date: May 2026. Duration: 56 minutes. Severity: SEV2.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Summary) Tj T*
(Customers saw errors from cart-api for 56 minutes. The trigger was thread pool starvation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Timeline) Tj T*
(09:12 alert fired. 09:20 incident declared. 09:35 mitigation applied.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Root cause) Tj T*
(A change merged two days earlier removed a safety limit, so thread pool starvation was able to) Tj T*
(build up unnoticed until peak traffic. Monitoring did not alert early because the threshold was) Tj T*
(set for the old traffic pattern.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Contributing factors) Tj T*
(- The runbook pointed to a dashboard that had been renamed.) Tj T*
(- The canary stage was skipped for a config-only change.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Action items) Tj T*
(- AI-275: restore the safety limit and add a regression test.) Tj T*
(- AI-646: update the alert threshold to the new traffic pattern.) Tj T*
(- AI-846: never skip the canary, including for config changes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
